# Commits that only moved whitespace around. `git blame` skips these and reports the commit that
# last changed a line's *content*, which is almost always the one you were looking for.
#
# GitHub honours this file automatically in its blame view. Locally it needs one config, which the
# root `prepare` script sets on `pnpm install`:
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a revision here if it is purely mechanical — a formatter run, a rename, an indentation
# change. A commit that also changes behaviour must never be listed: blame would then skip past
# the real author of that behaviour and point somewhere misleading.
#
# Entries need the full 40-character SHA; git rejects abbreviated ones.

# Add Prettier and EditorConfig, and format the codebase.
#
# Measured: this reformat is attributed only 70 lines repo-wide, and every one of them is a closing
# bracket or a blank line that the reflow genuinely created — so ignoring it reattributes nothing
